{"@type": "WebPage", "author": {"name": "Li Z.", "image": {"url": "https://media.licdn.com/dms/image/v2/C4E03AQFXcT0DFo4LGw/profile-displayphoto-shrink_400_400/profile-displayphoto-shrink_400_400/0/1647224204090?e=2147483647&v=beta&t=EfrrMkiPLoRg68JEJBHgape33zsy7Kbh8yoFLg1aAos", "@type": "ImageObject"}, "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/in/lizhounyc", "@type": "Person", "interactionStatistic": {"@type": "InteractionCounter", "interactionType": "http://schema.org/FollowAction", "userInteractionCount": 1558}}, "headline": "The Secretary-General has just released his Policy Brief “Valuing What Counts: Framework to Progress Beyond GDP” as part of the process leading up to the Summit of the Future. As the pandemic, the climate crisis, rising inequalities, and conflcits around the world remind us everyday, we need to have the right incentives and measures to maximise wellbeing for people and planet, not just production at the expense of everything else. 

This Policy Brief was based on the longer “Valuing What Counts” report requested by CEB which you can read here: https://lnkd.in/ePedmun8 

It’s been an incredible journey to have worked with brilliant thinkers (Maaike Jansen  Anu Peltola George Gray Molina Chantal Line Carpentier Stefan Schweinfest) across the UN to steer the development of this framework. Now the hard work begins!"}

