https://lnkd.in/eKuT-ftz"}

{"@type": "WebPage", "author": {"name": "Pradeep Kurukulasuriya", "image": {"url": "https://media.licdn.com/dms/image/v2/D4E03AQGhmJIBVBGEtg/profile-displayphoto-shrink_400_400/profile-displayphoto-shrink_400_400/0/1683321356186?e=2147483647&v=beta&t=4MBLqDHjXygv0COvIsYE_G3hRjgp6qqFwPHAmMxzJbA", "@type": "ImageObject"}, "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/in/pradeep-kurukulasuriya", "@type": "Person", "interactionStatistic": {"@type": "InteractionCounter", "interactionType": "http://schema.org/FollowAction", "userInteractionCount": 10021}}, "headline": "Energy has featured at the #AfricaClimateSummit and there is no doubt that unless we are collectively working to address the issue of energy access in off-grid settings, a whole of other "must-have's" on development, addressing inequality, not to mention addressing climate action and nature loss, is simply not possible. Words must turn into action. 

Here is an example of how my colleagues, Riad Meddeb and Mateo Salomon, and colleagues in UNDP Nigeria, in partnership with the Rural Electrification Agency of Nigeria, the Global Environment Facility, African Development Bank, Rocky Mountain Institute, and many other partners, most importantly, the communities in Kano, are going about things. A small step in the grand scheme of things, we kid ourselves not. Nonetheless,  if we can make things like this happen, we need to do more of it at scale and fast. 

That, can only happen if we all work together. We can and must. Let's just get it done."}

{"@type": "WebPage", "author": {"name": "Riad Meddeb", "image": {"url": "https://media.licdn.com/dms/image/v2/C5103AQG9sw02Vw5GAQ/profile-displayphoto-shrink_400_400/profile-displayphoto-shrink_400_400/0/1516239304664?e=2147483647&v=beta&t=XHzXiAvtB2oc4S_5p8foeQ7csNcNOh5JEyQ6pj75BN8", "@type": "ImageObject"}, "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/in/riadmeddeb", "@type": "Person", "interactionStatistic": {"@type": "InteractionCounter", "interactionType": "http://schema.org/FollowAction", "userInteractionCount": 17184}}, "headline": "Beyond just expanding youth voices in guiding #energy transition, UNDP  is developing an ecosystem of financial and technical support for youth innovation.

Never underestimate the critical role of #youth innovators and entrepreneurs leading solutions in the #JustEnergyTransition
#IRENA"}

caption:
Ending hunger and tackling the climate crisis are deeply interconnected; and energy sits at the nexus of both.  

Energy is the backbone of agrifood systems, powering the entire value chain from production and processing to storage and distribution. Today, these systems consume 30% of global energy and account for 31% of food system-related emissions; yet receive <4% of global climate finance. Without urgent investment in clean, reliable and affordable energy, agrifood systems will continue to drive emissions, food loss and deepen rural inequalities.  

But solutions exist, and they are already making a difference: 👉 https://lnkd.in/eNH_Vefp

Renewable energy, sustainable bioenergy and energy-efficient technologies are powering irrigation, cold storage and processing. From 2011 to 2021, the share of renewable energy in the agriculture, forestry & fisheries from 10.8% to 15.4%. Off-grid solar has reached over 560 million people and cold chain expansion is helping cut the 13% of food lost post-harvest. These solutions already reduce emissions, cut food waste and unlock opportunities for women and youth. Solar-powered cold chains, decentralized minigrids, agrivoltaics and clean cooking solutions are not just innovations; they are lifelines for rural transformation. To realize this potential, we should: 

🌾 Scale up investment through blended finance and targeted support for smallholders;  

🌾 Embed energy-smart agrifood systems into national policies, NDCs, and development strategies;  

🌾 Foster cross-sector collaboration between energy, agriculture, water, and climate actors;  

🌾Invest in data, training, and resilient infrastructure to ensure long-term impact. 
 
Clean energy is not a side issue. It is essential to feed a growing population and stay within our planetary boundaries. With coordinated action, inclusive finance and enhanced political will, we can transform agrifood systems into engines of food security, rural development and climate resilience.  

#EnergyForDevelopment #HLPF2025 #SDG2 #SDG7 #FoodSecurity #AgriFoodSystems

